.dev/reviews/405-knowledge/codex.out:612:- For the chat API, SSE should use safe framing such as JSON or other line-safe payloads, and long-lived streams should not hold request-scoped DB sessions open after DB access is no longer needed [Task 2]
.dev/reviews/405-knowledge/codex.out:616:- For node overrides, the strongest confidence comes from proving effect in both API-level verifiers and browser e2e: UI override applied, trace changes, tool-call count actually drops [Task 4]
.dev/reviews/405-knowledge/codex.out:624:- Symptom: SSE/chat logic is fragile or unsafe. Cause: raw token text was streamed directly and validation stayed loose. Fix: use safe framing and typed schema validation, and close DB sessions before streaming when possible [Task 2]
